    "method": "each route path (dynamic segments substituted with a literal sample) evaluated through the three real gate matchers, in the same nesting order app/layout.tsx renders them: InternalSurfaceGate (lib/internalSurfaces.ts#isInternalSurface) > FocusChromeGate (lib/focusRoutes.ts#isFocusRoute) > B2BChromeGate (components/B2BLayout.tsx#isB2BRoute, reimplemented here verbatim since it lives in a client component). First match wins; a route reaching none of the three keeps global chrome."
  },
  "mechanism": {
    "routeGroups": false,
    "nestedLayoutFiles": 1,
    "nestedLayoutFilesList": [
      "app/layout.tsx"
    ],
    "gateComponents": [
      "components/InternalSurfaceGate.tsx",
      "components/FocusLayout.tsx (FocusChromeGate)",
      "components/B2BLayout.tsx (B2BChromeGate)"
    ],
    "note": "Shell selection is imperative, not structural. There is no app/(global|focus|b2b) route-group partition P0 §9 asks for. Instead, one root layout renders Header/Footer/MobileBottomNav/MiniCartBar wrapped in three nested client-side gates, each a usePathname() check that returns null to un-render the chrome. A separate, independent mechanism (an inline <head> script serialising STITCH_EXACT_ROUTES/STITCH_PREFIX_ROUTES and FOCUS_ROUTES/INTERNAL_ROUTES) stamps data-stitch=\"dark\" on <html> and data-focus-route=\"true\" on <body> before hydration, for zero-flash CSS purposes only — it does not un-render anything and is not a fourth shell.",
    "b2bShellIsRealChrome": "false — B2BChromeGate un-renders the global chrome on B2B routes but nothing replaces it. The 10 B2B-classified routes render with NO header, footer, or nav of any kind. The component's own comment (\"the B2B layout will render its own specialized chrome\") does not match what ships: grep for Header/Nav usage inside app/corporate, app/group, app/office-lunch, app/rd-partners, app/partners finds none."
  },
  "defects": [
    {
      "id": "b2b-boundary-bug",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "components/B2BLayout.tsx#isB2BRoute uses raw pathname.startsWith(\"/corporate\") with no trailing-slash boundary check, unlike isFocusRoute and isInternalSurface which both check `path === route || path.startsWith(route + \"/\")`. Consequence: /corporate-wellness incorrectly matches as a B2B route and loses its global chrome (Header/Footer/MobileBottomNav) even though it is a standalone marketing page, not part of the /corporate family.",
      "affectedRoute": "/corporate-wellness",
      "fix": "Match the boundary-aware pattern the other two matchers already use."
    },
    {
      "id": "b2b-no-replacement-chrome",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "10 routes (the /corporate*, /group, /office-lunch, /rd-partners, /partners family) render with zero navigation chrome — no Header, no Footer, no MobileBottomNav, and no B2B-specific replacement despite the gate component's own comment promising one. A visitor on any of these pages has no way to navigate elsewhere in the app except the browser back button.",
      "affectedRoutes": "see routes.json totals.byShell[\"b2b-chrome-suppressed\"]"
    }
  ],
